[0m[0m
The C code's fallthrough switch does shifts on [38;5;10mint[0m (implicit promotion from [38;5;10munsigned char[0m). For [38;5;10mcase 4: data |= (d[3] << 24)[0m, when [38;5;10md[3] = 0xFF[0m, the shift produces [38;5;10m0xFF000000[0m which is negative as [38;5;10mint32[0m. When widened to [38;5;10msize_t[0m (64-bit), it sign-extends to [38;5;10m0xFFFFFFFFFF000000[0m. The Rust code was casting to [38;5;10musize[0m first, producing [38;5;10m0x00000000FF000000[0m — no sign extension.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fix: Cast to [38;5;10mi32[0m before shifting for cases 4, 3, 2 to match C's integer promotion rules:[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10m// Before (wrong):
if rem >= 4 { data |= (*dp.add(3) as usize) << 24; }
// After (correct):
if rem >= 4 { data |= ((*dp.add(3) as i32) << 24) as usize; }
